mcommander is built from a release archive created by
packaging/release-source.sh.  The archive deliberately contains .tarball-version:
version.sh reads the version from Git in a checkout, and outside Git the build
would otherwise report it as "unknown".

This directory carries no version.  debian/changelog is generated by
packaging/prepare.sh from the annotated v* tags, and is listed in .gitignore.
Its entries are the tag messages and its dates are the tag dates, so the same
tag always yields the same source package.

The package declares Replaces: mc6 and nothing else. mc6 was an earlier name of
this program, published in a PPA of its own and retired. The two share one path,
/usr/bin/mctree, and without Replaces dpkg refuses to unpack over it. They can
be installed side by side otherwise, so no Conflicts and no Breaks is needed,
and the relation carries no version because mc6 has no further releases.

To build the source package for a version, take the release archive and copy
this directory into it.  Building from the Git checkout instead would add the
whole of packaging/ as a patch, and record the absence of .tarball-version:

  packaging/release-source.sh 6.0.3 v6.0.3
  packaging/prepare.sh 6.0.3 dist/mcommander-6.0.3.tar.gz
  tar -xf dist/mcommander-6.0.3.tar.gz -C /tmp
  cp dist/mcommander-6.0.3.tar.gz /tmp/mcommander_6.0.3.orig.tar.gz
  cp -r debian /tmp/mcommander-6.0.3/
  cd /tmp/mcommander-6.0.3 && dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc

A version without a tag of its own is a test build: prepare.sh marks its entry
UNRELEASED, and dput refuses such a package.  For a PPA, name the target series
and add a series suffix to the version:

  DEB_DISTRIBUTION=noble DEB_VERSION_SUFFIX='~ubuntu24.04.1' \
      packaging/prepare.sh 6.0.3 dist/mcommander-6.0.3.tar.gz

Files taken from gnulib
-----------------------

lib/strutil/filevercmp.c and lib/strutil/strverscmp.c come from gnulib, which
is a source library: it is copied into a tree and built with it, and there is
no shared library to link against instead. The Debian gnulib package is Architecture: all and carries sources
only. The files here were taken by hand, not with gnulib-tool, which is why the
tree has no bootstrap.conf and no gnulib-cache.m4, and why their vintage
differs from file to file; the years are in each header. They are adapted to
this tree: strverscmp.c includes config.h and lib/strutil.h and carries a
second notice of its own. Every one of them is declared in debian/copyright
with the license of its own, LGPL-2.1+ or LGPL-3+, not the GPL-3+ of the rest.

Generated files in the archive
------------------------------

The release archive carries no generated build files: it is the tree of the
tag plus .tarball-version, and the build runs meson on it.
